A||||11||mshill||Tough shifting into reverse...||||9
Z||000000||mshill||10-26-1999||03:46 PM||||I have an 86 SE V6 Manual 4 speed.  I just finished bleeding the clutch properly, but it is still very difficult to get into reverse.<P>It is not that the tranny doesn't want to go into reverse, but it seems I have to really yank on the stick to get it over (to the left) to where I can stick it into reverse.  It seems to be a linkage problem and I really don't think it should be this hard.<P>Is it a linkage adjustment? Or is my linkage just shot?<BR>||||reg||9
Z||000001||WGraffiKs||10-26-1999||04:37 PM||||Have you tried aligning the shift linkage yet?  My haynes manual suggests doing this to cure shift harshness into/between 1st and reverse.  It's pretty easy, too.<BR>There is supposed to be a bit of extra resistance (shifting to the left) into the reverse notch.  It's there to prevent unintentional shifts into reverse when moving forward, but it should not be excessive.<BR>Bill||||reg||1
Z||000002||Greg Piet||10-26-1999||04:41 PM||||I just got my 4speed re done.  It does need a  bit of a "kick" to get it to go all  the way to the left to get it into reverse.  This was exemplified when I put in a short shifter.  Normally I give it a firm, but smooth kick over to the left but then pressing forward into Reverse is effortless.  The Isuzu's tranny isnt the smoothest in town, so I am rather used to it being a bit finnicky.<P>PS I initially the word kick was "krej" in reversed order but it got automatically bleeped.  Hmmmm  very odd!<p>[This message has been edited by Greg Piet (edited 10-26-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||mshill||10-26-1999||04:42 PM||||I will check my Haynes manual tonight.  It is so hard to get into reverse that my wife can't drive the car.<P>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000004||Patrick||10-26-1999||05:27 PM||||<BR>mshill, so.... is that a problem?||||reg||10
Z||000005||mshill||10-26-1999||05:47 PM||||patrick,<P>my selfish response would be 'No, not a problem.'  But since she is the one who encouraged me to find a sporty two seater, and the one who has to come out to the garage to talk to me, I think she should be able to enjoy it as well.<P>She likes the car, and she certainly get tired of driving the GMC Safari Van around full of kids.  She is entitled to have some fun as well.<P>||||reg||1
