Z||000007||FieroSTETZ||10-26-1999||10:43 PM||||i have a very hard time shifting into first and reverse as well... it grinds when i try to go to reverse (im not just bad at it, no one can do it without grinding it unless they turn off the car) is this probably my linkage? (i have full hydraulic fluid and the clutch was bled)||||reg||1
Z||000008||Bruce||10-26-1999||11:06 PM||||Somewhere in the archives of this forum is the topic about "difficult shifting." I had the same problem (tough to get into 3rd, reverse wouldn't go over far enough to activate the back-up light). I took a copy of the suggestions from the forum, had the linkage adjusted, and it shifts great. Something wears out and has to be turned 180 degrees. Check thru the topics!!||||reg||1
Z||000009||Drako||10-28-1999||01:13 PM||||I had the same problem your having before I took my 84 4spd 4cyl off the road to give it  a 63 buick v8.... Whenever I tried to go into reverse from neutral it would grind, but if I took it into second then to reverse it was fine, it was extremly strange. I can't tell you much more because I only drove the car for about a week before I took it off the road to give it a swap and its still in the garage getting its swap.<P>Drako (Roy)||||reg||8
Z||000010||mwbackus||10-28-1999||04:34 PM||||Not sure about the other trannys, but the getrag does not have a synchro on reverse gear.  To select reverse without grinding it, shift into 3rd (or 4th) first, then go to reverse.  The shift will stop the movement so that the reverse gears will mesh.<p>[This message has been edited by mwbackus (edited 10-28-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||mshill||10-28-1999||04:38 PM||||Well, I got the shift linkage adjusted per the Haynes manual.  I also greased all the moving parts of the shifter.  It now shifts smoothly over to reverse.<P>However, I was diappointed to find that my master cylinder (just rebuilt a month ago) is leaking out the front seal. I HATE HYDROLIC CLUTCHES!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!<P>I think it needs a new clutch anyway, so I am going to drop the engine for the rebuild and get a clutch and have the transmission serviced while it is out.<BR>||||reg||9
